WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:04.370
There are hundreds of scripted television
series, and with cable channels, streaming

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:09.280
services, and even tech companies like Facebook
and Apple creating their own original programming,

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.780
the list of TV options is only getting more
crowded.

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:16.430
Network TV might not be the trendiest destination
these days, but after all these decades, they

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:17.590
still know what they're doing.

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:22.369
In fact, the networks still produce consistently
impressive content, even if much of it seems

00:00:22.369 --> 00:00:23.570
to get lost in the shuffle.

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:28.359
Here are some of the best network TV shows
that nobody's talking about.

00:00:28.359 --> 00:00:29.779
Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:00:29.779 --> 00:00:33.680
If you stopped watching ABC's Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.
after its first season, it's high time to

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:34.800
get back on board.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:38.680
The Marvel series resurrects the character
Phil Coulson to lead a team of S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:41.430
agents who have to deal with an array of small-screen
villains.

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:44.950
The show has been able to pick up some of
the weirder and more obscure corners of Marvel

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:49.589
Comics that are passed over in the films,
making it a great series for fans of the comics

00:00:49.589 --> 00:00:53.739
— and its fun plotting and likable characters
make it worth a watch even for people who

00:00:53.739 --> 00:00:55.140
aren't comic book readers.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:58.420
"Did you just give me a compliment?"

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:02.820
The show's sixth season is set to return in
the summer of 2019, after the release of Avengers

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:07.060
4, giving viewers who haven't seen the series
plenty of time to catch up on this hidden

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:08.310
gem.

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:09.830
Fresh Off the Boat

00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:12.620
ABC has some major hits in their family comedy
block.

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:16.621
In addition to the highly acclaimed sitcoms
Modern Family and Black-ish, the network's

00:01:16.621 --> 00:01:21.290
best household may be in the delightful 1990s-set
sitcom Fresh Off the Boat.

00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:25.650
The show stars the always brilliant Constance
Wu as an uptight Taiwanese immigrant raising

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:27.510
three boys in Orlando, Florida.

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:31.830
Recent seasons have flown largely under the
radar, but with one of the best casts in comedy

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:35.750
television, Fresh Off the Boat remains must-see
TV.

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:37.220
Good Girls

00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:41.930
Men have gotten their fair share of TV anti-heroes,
but women finally got theirs in NBC's Good

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:42.660
Girls.

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:44.880
"Ladies and gentlemen, this is a robbery."

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:48.880
The crime drama series centers around three
moms who get in over their heads after robbing

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:50.310
a local grocery store.

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:54.120
The cast is brilliant, and the many plot twists
keep the show moving at a swift pace.

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:58.290
Good Girls was met with moderate reviews from
critics at the start, but continued to improve

00:01:58.290 --> 00:02:02.230
throughout its run, eventually earning an
"A" rating from Entertainment Weekly for its

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:03.580
season one finale.

00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:07.630
It's hard to predict where the show will go
next, which makes it exactly the kind of fun,

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:09.910
soapy ride you want to get on.

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:11.500
Speechless

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:15.580
It's not easy to successfully combine heart
and humor, but that's precisely what the ABC

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:17.430
sitcom Speechless has done.

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:21.370
The series follows a family whose oldest son
has cerebral palsy, leaving him, as the show's

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:23.480
title suggests, speechless.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:26.760
Critics have noted that the show's handling
of the character's disability is impressive,

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:28.350
with an IndieWire review saying,

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:34.070
"[The show is] actively anti-tokenism [and]
exemplifies simple human decency without emphasizing

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:35.070
it."

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:38.270
With a talented cast led by Minnie Driver
as the family's matriarch, Speechless is a

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:40.680
comedy gem you don't want to miss.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:41.680
Superstore

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:46.440
There are a lot of workplace comedies, so
it's easy for some to get lost in the shuffle,

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:49.580
but NBC's Superstore definitely deserves a
closer look.

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:53.940
The show stars Golden Globe winner America
Ferrera as an employee at the fictional superstore

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:54.990
Cloud 9.

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:59.410
Despite the familiarity of its premise, Superstore
has been consistently funny throughout its

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:01.800
run, and boasts a diverse, hilarious cast.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:05.430
The series may not have the biggest star power,
but it's one of the most reliable comedies

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:07.330
on TV when you really need a laugh.

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:08.630
"This is amazing."

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:12.640
"Yeah, I'm generally a cynic, but this…
wow."

00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:15.160
Trial and Error

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:19.710
The courtroom is always ripe for drama, but
it hasn't inspired many modern comedy series.

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:23.800
NBC filled that hole with their legal anthology
mockumentary Trial and Error, which features

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:28.120
a young lawyer and an assistant district attorney
who try New York's toughest cases.

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:32.250
Aside from the show's ability to recruit big
stars, it's also earned positive reviews from

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:33.250
critics.

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:35.959
"Is this something people have been talking
about?"

00:03:35.959 --> 00:03:36.959
"Well…"

00:03:36.959 --> 00:03:40.530
With a wacky sense of humor, Trial and Error
often gets much more bizarre than its premise

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:45.380
would suggest, making each episode a hilarious
comedic surprise.

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:46.590
iZombie

00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:49.620
Comic book properties may be all the rage,
but most viewers are sleeping on one of the

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:51.860
best comic book adaptations on TV.

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:57.400
The CW's iZombie is a smart, funny, and quick-witted
adaptation of the Vertigo series of the same

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:58.400
name.

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:01.580
In the iZombie universe, eating someone's
brains gives you a hint about how they passed

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:05.800
away, and medical examiner Liv, who happens
to be a zombie, uses her skill to assist the

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:09.390
Seattle Police Department in solving their
most difficult cases.

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:12.970
iZombie's procedural elements are a consistent
delight, but what has made the series truly

00:04:12.970 --> 00:04:14.850
great is the expansion of its world.

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:19.540
Balancing week-to-week storylines with season-long
storylines, the show boasts compelling characters

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:20.540
and fun romance.

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:21.540
Thanks for watching!

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:24.470
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:26.750
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

